<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monterado</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Monterado is a town in Bengkayang Regency, West Kalimantan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, inland from Singkawang. In the 18th and 19th centuries it was a centre of Chinese gold mining in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> and the seat of the Heshun federation of mining kongsis, dominated by the Dagang kongsi, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> dissolved it in the Kongsi Wars of 1850–1854.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/monterado.jpg" alt="Monterado" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pere Garcia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pgr_Monterado_-_Castello_di_Monterado.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
